      "final_answer": "**One finding:** the comment at `brainspace_copilot_bridge.py:124\u2013126` says MD-1 \u201conly adds\u201d to regex routing, but lines 355\u2013359 let valid below-threshold scores **suppress regex matches**. Existing tests explicitly expect that behavior; the comment is stale.\n\n- `_AGENT_COMMANDS` contains `fleet`, `review`, `security-review`, and `research`. Leading commands keep agent tools regardless of MD-1 scores; `/fleet` also keeps SQL. `/rubber-duck` is deliberately excluded as unconfirmed.\n- `MD1_THRESHOLD` defaults to `0.5`, with inclusive `>=` comparison. Environment overrides accept finite values in `[0, 1]`; invalid values revert to the default. Missing or invalid family scores fall back to regex routing.\n\nRepository untouched.",
