      "final_answer": "`STARTUP` is **two minutes** (`brainspace_copilot_bridge.py:123`). It bounds fallback session-to-launch matching, not subagent/workflow intent detection.\n\nAt lines 460\u2013466, matching requires:\n- Same working directory and `launch.start < session.created_at <= min(launch.end, launch.start + STARTUP)`.\n- Exactly one matching launch, with no competing session in that window. Explicit session-ID matches bypass the window.\n\n**Routing consequence:** a missed or ambiguous match causes fresh tool selection instead of restoring recorded exclusions. A successful match preserves exclusions by default\u2014even for new agent/workflow requests\u2014unless `TOKENMASTER_RESUME_ESCALATE` is enabled (lines 498\u2013505).\n\nThe window uses session creation time, so a delayed first message is harmless. Creation after two minutes\u2014or exactly equal to launch start\u2014does not match. These are heuristic boundaries, not confirmed defects. Repository untouched.",
